1
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:04,220
I knew the man was crazy,
but not that crazy!

2
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:16,450
Straightzo!

3
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:19,537
I'm going to give you a choice on
how you want to meet your demise.

4
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,697
Will it be plain old sunlight or Hamon?

5
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:23,497
Or I could just smash in your brains!

6
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:25,345
How would you feel about that?

7
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,297
He's going to kill us all!

8
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,210
Huh?

9
00:00:31,293 --> 00:00:33,960
Jojo, would you lose your mind?

10
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:35,885
Just look at what you've done!

11
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:40,900
Yeah, I know.

12
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:43,577
It'll take a small fortune to
fix everything in this place.

13
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:44,490
Not that!

14
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:46,380
You just shot a person!

15
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:47,730
Person?

16
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:50,060
You mean straighter?

17
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:54,777
These bullets I fired at him
all have strange dents in them.

18
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:56,684
They've been completely warped.

19
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,346
Smokey, get out of here, now.

20
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:03,660
That thing I shot, I can only
hope that he was a person.

21
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:08,940
And if he was, I'll happily go to jail
without thinking twice about it. What?

22
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:09,910
I don't...

23
00:01:09,993 --> 00:01:10,877
What else would he be?

24
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,880
Can we please stop the crying?

25
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:14,277
I'm trying to think here.

26
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:17,654
If you don't calm down, I may
have to make out with you.

27
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:31,200
I don't know.

28
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,377
Thank

29
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:18,460
you.

30
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:48,820
Thank you.

31
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:36,117
Dio's failure was in his
infatuation with his own power.

32
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:39,720
He just couldn't resist
constantly pushing his own limits.

33
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:43,531
He stretched himself thin,
allowing Jonathan to strike him.

34
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,880
But I have a different philosophy.

35
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:48,717
I figure I'll have plenty
of time to reflect on

36
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,357
the extent of my powers
after you're destroyed.

37
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:53,400
There will be no mercy for you.

38
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:56,017
I thought it would be
appropriate to open up

39
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:59,041
with the technique that
Dio used to kill Jonathan.

40
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:04,637
Guns will fail.

41
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:09,000
However, I can fire high-pressure
essence from my eyes.

42
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:13,000
Look deeply into my space-ripper's
stingy eyes, Joseph!

43
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:17,870
JoJo!

44
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:20,760
That was a little too easy.

45
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:23,820
Now, the only one left is Arena Joestar.

46
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,397
And that should be...

47
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,677
I know what you'll say next.

48
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:29,340
About as easy as taking candy from a baby.

49
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:32,810
Hmm.

50
00:04:32,893 --> 00:04:34,337
Next thing you'll say is...

51
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:37,357
How could he possibly be alive
with that hole in his head?

52
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:38,270
Am I right?

53
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:42,187
But how could he possibly be
alive with that hole in his head?

54
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:47,757
Too much time meditating out in the
Tibetan boonies has dulled your senses.

55
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,317
That's why I like this city.

56
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,518
It keeps you sharp.

57
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:54,957
You wouldn't be so confused right now if
you had just been a bit more observant.

58
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,511
All right, here's a hint.

59
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:59,504
You wouldn't happen to
have the time, would you?

60
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:04,120
I heard the story about Dio
taking down my grandfather.

61
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:07,720
by firing some sort of blast
from his eyes. A mirror!

62
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,520
Look who finally noticed!

63
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,220
Straight, Zof!

64
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:14,257
I also heard that you
may be severely allergic

65
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:16,987
to Hamon just as much
as you are to sunlight!

66
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,680
Batter up!

67
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:22,400
Here comes the pinch!

68
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,600
Let's out of here! Yeah!

69
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:36,160
So, I hear that Hamon does a pretty
good job of melting vampire faces.

70
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:37,840
Let's have a look here.

71
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:52,200
He's unharmed!

72
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:55,257
It's as though I never
even touched him at all.

73
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:57,757
Could it be possible
that Granny was wrong?

74
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:58,820
Not at all.

75
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:00,717
Your Granny was not wrong,

76
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,857
because I can see that
you would grow into quite

77
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:05,700
a worthy foe if I didn't
have to kill you now.

78
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,000
Here's a secret before you die.

79
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:13,220
There is an insect deep in Southeast
Asia called the Sariporosia beetle.

80
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:16,157
Thirty thousand of
their tiny stomachs have

81
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:18,657
been dried out and then
woven into this scarf.

82
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:22,940
Their bodies conduct Harmon
far better than a human body,

83
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:24,748
thus dispersing the charge.

84
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:27,100
It's similar to an electrical ground.

85
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:32,320
I have inherited 4,000 years worth of
history and research in the art of Harmon.

86
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:35,420
Unlike Dio, I have studied the craft.

87
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:39,405
I am a master of its strengths
and flaws in all forms of combat.

88
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:43,360
Wow, that's quite impressive.
No, really? It is.

89
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:47,737
But did you think I'd completely rely on
a gimmick like Harmon all of the time?

90
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:54,357
Hmm hmm I'm also very fast what how

91
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:56,558
did you pin that grenade on my scarf

92
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:02,517
Child's play sure but I was still
able to pull one over on you wasn't

93
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:06,424
I and you Should take a look at
the grenade you just knocked away

94
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:09,180
You son of a

95
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:18,650
Oh!

96
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:25,480
Well, that was a close one.

97
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:32,750
Wha...

98
00:07:32,833 --> 00:07:33,960
what the hell is he?

99
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,837
Smokey, I thought I told you to run.

100
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,477
It's too late for that now.

101
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:42,120
Please, God, I promise I won't
ever do anything bad again.

102
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:44,440
No stealing, no lying, I swear it.

103
00:07:44,780 --> 00:07:46,500
Please, just save me.

104
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:04,370
He...

105
00:08:04,453 --> 00:08:05,283
He's a monster.

106
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:14,797
You probably kill monsters all the time.

107
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:16,097
You know what to do, right?

108
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,010
Jojo?

109
00:08:17,093 --> 00:08:19,280
Sure, of course I do. Great!

110
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,080
I knew you would! Yep.

111
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:24,320
I have a secret weapon for
situations such as this.

112
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,540
A secret weapon? Really?

113
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:27,936
What kind of weapon?

114
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,480
Why isn't it obvious?

115
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:31,740
Look at his legs, Smokey.

116
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:35,817
I basically blew them to smithereens,
and they still haven't fully healed yet.

117
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:37,253
That's our ticket then.

118
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:40,107
What do his legs have
to do with your weapon?

119
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:42,040
My legs are in great shape.

120
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:44,201
So what are you going to do then?

121
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,680
Run as fast as I can!

122
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,380
Make way! Move!

123
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:49,622
Out of the way!

124
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:50,939
This guy's insane!

125
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:57,500
Come on, follow me, straight zone.

126
00:08:57,960 --> 00:09:00,020
Hey, wait up! Jojo!

127
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:07,360
I will make him pay dearly for that.

128
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:08,797
Even though I'm immortal,

129
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:12,351
it'll take some time to regenerate
after what he did to me.

130
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,400
This is a perfect scoop.

131
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:17,917
The papers will be falling
all over themselves.

132
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,037
This is my chance to break
into big-time journalism.

133
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:25,460
Pressure applied by fingertips, 235
kilograms per centimeter squared.

134
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:31,480
Leaping ability, currently
4 meters 22 centimeters.

135
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,500
It's behind me, isn't it?

136
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,880
We should be safe by now, right?

137
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:51,260
I'm afraid not, Smokey.

138
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:52,460
Do you hear that?

139
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,160
Do I hear what, Jojo?

140
00:09:54,540 --> 00:09:56,437
The only thing I hear is the river.

141
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:58,420
No, not that. Look up!

142
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,880
He followed us here!

143
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,180
Run, Jojo, run!

144
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:09,800
I would not do that if I were you.

145
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:12,660
Run away and I'll kill her right here.

146
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:16,120
But come up and meet me,
and I will let her go.

147
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:17,957
What sort of threat is that?

148
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:20,840
I don't even know who
that woman is, you moron.

149
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:22,200
Jojo, let's run!

150
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:25,357
Whether you know this woman
or not is inconsequential.

151
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:28,793
If you flee now, I'll know
just what sort of man you are.

152
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:32,617
Rather than pursue you, I could
use this time to heal myself.

153
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:36,940
For a true coward would not seek
revenge for Speedwagon. However,

154
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:40,597
if you were to come up here
after a girl you don't even know,

155
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:43,277
then I'll see that you
are both courageous and

156
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:47,017
powerful which means you'll
present a real threat!

157
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:50,957
and continue to pursue me into the
future and I would therefore have to

158
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:54,577
eliminate you here and now I'll kill

159
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:59,180
her regardless fight me or run decide?

160
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:19,337
Go ahead and do what you think
you need to do, straightzo.

161
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:22,617
I wouldn't fight for that floozy
even if I was married to her.

162
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:26,357
Are you certain that this is the
type of game you wish to play?

163
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:28,957
It would be so easy to
tear through her neck and

164
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:31,805
open up her chest cavity
with just two fingers.

165
00:11:36,180 --> 00:11:39,537
A true master of Tibetan Hamon
would never do such a thing.

166
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:42,700
Such gratuitous cruelty would be unseemly.

167
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:53,930
That...

168
00:11:54,013 --> 00:11:54,843
that was a tooth!

169
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,077
He just ripped it right out of her mouth!

170
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,480
Just despicable.

171
00:11:58,820 --> 00:12:00,920
This bastard has no conscience.

172
00:12:01,740 --> 00:12:04,080
Consider that your last warning.

173
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,440
You demonic freak.

174
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:13,240
Release her strikes out!

175
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:18,580
You pay for that!

176
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,420
You're a vile inhuman abomination!

177
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:27,500
Your act of playing it calm belies
the fire that we see in you now.

178
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,900
Let's skip the pretty speeches!

179
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,120
Now you're mine!

180
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:36,980
Take this!

181
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:38,460
Oh no!

182
00:12:39,620 --> 00:12:41,480
Fool me once, then shame on me.

183
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:46,388
But unfortunately for you, straight-so,
you'll never be able to fool me twice!

184
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:47,970
Hamon!

185
00:12:58,040 --> 00:12:58,870
That's him!

186
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:01,157
Now you'll say that's impossible!

187
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,299
That's impossible!

188
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:07,077
I deflected your shot with
a little Hamon shot glass.

189
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:10,260
I was pretty sure you'd
go for my forehead again.

190
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:13,289
Predictability can be
quite the fatal flaw.

191
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:24,660
Give my best to Speedwagon and Howl!

192
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:31,080
Granny should be able to
sleep well tonight. Finally.

193
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:47,920
Why would you try to save me from falling?

194
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:50,417
Aren't you frightened that I still possess

195
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:53,360
enough power in me to
blow your arm clean off?

196
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:55,320
I'd like to see you try that.

197
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:59,011
I'll just pummel you into
fertilizer with my remaining arm.

198
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:01,240
I want some answers, Straightzo.

199
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:04,997
Tell me, why did you throw
Speedwagon's body into the river?

200
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:07,139
Something here just doesn't add up.

201
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:11,400
Joseph, your grandfather
Jonathan's blood flows through you.

202
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:16,460
From the outside, you appear to be opposites,
but you're both insatiably curious.

203
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:20,317
And now it is my pleasure
to warn you that your nature

204
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:23,740
has trapped you in a fate
you cannot hope to escape.

205
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:26,868
What are you talking about?

206
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:28,660
Soon you shall learn of him,

207
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:33,500
of the Pillar Man, and then you shall
finally come face to face with him.

208
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:34,630
Oh, shut up!

209
00:14:34,713 --> 00:14:37,077
I'm done decoding your
rubbish straight, though.

210
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:40,017
But I threw the bodies into
the river because of him.

211
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:41,420
Don't you see, fool?

212
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:46,100
The pillar sucked deeply of the
blood from those bodies in the cave.

213
00:14:46,540 --> 00:14:49,700
It was like a plant ravenously
drawing in nutrients.

214
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:54,160
It was ghastly, so I
dragged the bodies outside.

215
00:14:54,600 --> 00:15:00,900
But I have no doubts now that he will
soon awaken from his 2,000-year slumber.

216
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:07,160
Not to worry.

217
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:10,117
It is fated that you
shall meet him very soon.

218
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:11,920
And when that time comes,

219
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:15,826
you shall learn his identity and
the true meaning of evolution.

220
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:18,580
Your destiny has already been written.

221
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:23,300
Is that Harmon?

222
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:28,957
So that means you must have been
creating Harmon inside your own body.

223
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:32,417
There is nothing I regret
Joseph all this time.

224
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:35,237
I planned on entering hell
while still vibrant and

225
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:38,737
filled with energy not as some
withered desiccated corpse.

226
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:43,357
I cannot tell you the ecstasy that
I have felt in being young again.

227
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:45,337
Straits are wait not yet.

228
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:46,740
I need to know more

229
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:49,740
Farewell to you Jojo

230
00:15:58,540 --> 00:15:59,370
Jojo!

231
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:10,880
1938, the second world war rages,

232
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:13,117
threatening to engulf more
nations around the globe?

233
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,494
with each passing day.

234
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:18,137
As the German army grows, it seeks
to conquer the world with technology.

235
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:21,377
and weapons that stand at the
very cutting edge of science.

236
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:25,931
However, they also research astrology,
sorcery, alchemy, and psychic powers.

237
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:28,577
They seek to gain advantages
through every manner

238
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:31,484
imaginable in their quest
for global domination.

239
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:34,877
And it was through this
tenacity that one of their spy

240
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:38,078
networks in Mexico caught
wind of Straitzo's actions.

241
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:46,297
I'm so terribly sorry, Major von Stroheim.

242
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,540
My hand, it just slipped.

243
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:50,328
I don't know what happened.

244
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,110
Lick it.

245
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:58,100
You drew blood from me, no?

246
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:02,600
Don't make me order you to
lick my wound clean. Yes, sir.

247
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,300
Gently now.

248
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:09,057
I know you wouldn't want to hurt me again.

249
00:17:09,140 --> 00:17:09,970
Good.

250
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:12,220
Slowly now, slowly.

251
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:14,290
Hmm.

252
00:17:14,373 --> 00:17:16,840
I think the pain is going away. Now.

253
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:20,740
Be careful now!

254
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:21,997
Careful now!

255
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:23,460
Don't cut your tongue!

256
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:26,609
Pardon my interruption,
Major von Stroheim!

257
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:32,197
The old man found on the
bank of the Rio Dada!

258
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:34,257
He is now awake, Major von Stroheim!

259
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:35,869
Shall we interrogate, sir?

260
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,180
Are you alright, miss?

261
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,817
Can you tell me your name?

262
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:43,460
Allow me to escort you home, huh?

263
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:46,462
Why in the hell did you do that?

264
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:49,497
You've got some nerve calling
me a floozy, you big brute.

265
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:52,440
Just who do you think you
are anyway, huh? What?

266
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:53,700
I never said that.

267
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:55,160
No, you did.

268
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:58,872
You said that you would never
fight for a floozy like her.

269
00:17:59,020 --> 00:17:59,850
Really?

270
00:17:59,933 --> 00:18:01,140
Wow, I didn't mean it.

271
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:03,017
I'm really sorry about that.

272
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:04,629
It just happened, kind of.

273
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:09,924
Yeah, I'm sure it just happens
every time you talk about a woman.

274
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,480
Your mouth okay?

275
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:21,497
Looks like the adrenaline
from her fear just wore off.

276
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:25,992
Now it's time to find out about this
pillar man Straitzo was talking about.

277
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:28,860
I can't wait to see Mexico.

278
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:44,540
How are you feeling, Speedwagon?

279
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:48,260
There is a saying in
Europe that comes to mind.

280
00:18:48,820 --> 00:18:53,291
The village in which the elderly kill
each other is not long for this world.

281
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:58,340
You have a secret, a secret that is
very dangerous and could kill us all.

282
00:19:04,940 --> 00:19:06,820
I want answers now!

283
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:17,298
There appears to be a man
trapped inside this pillar.

284
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:21,340
We extracted it from the location
we got from you. Why, God?

285
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,820
Why do this to me?

286
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,517
Why couldn't you just have
let me die back there?

287
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:27,160
Why did you make me live?

288
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:30,080
It wasn't God, at least not your God.

289
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:34,200
I was the one who made you
live, but I can change that.

290
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:39,902
The Wehrmacht would like some information
from you before anything drastic happens.

291
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,180
You are stubborn old man.

292
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:45,697
I'm smart enough to
know that torture alone

293
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:48,117
would not give us what we want out of you.

294
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:51,797
I also know that you were penniless
when you first got to Texas.

295
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:55,277
You were nearly dead in the desert
when you found the oil fields

296
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:59,125
that would soon cause a massive
overhaul of the world's economy.

297
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:00,280
Get ready!

298
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:03,997
German medicine is the greatest
thing in the world, don't you think?

299
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:05,580
Speak and do anything!

300
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:07,260
A truth serum?

301
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:08,520
For what?

302
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:10,497
What more could you possibly want from me?

303
00:20:10,580 --> 00:20:11,480
Everything!

304
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:13,380
I want to know it all!

305
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:15,240
Give me a history lesson!

306
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:18,840
Tell me about Straitzo
and about this Joe Star.

307
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:22,480
Tell us so that we can
finally awaken the Pillar Man!

308
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:24,780
No, no, you can't!

309
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:26,957
You don't know the forces
you're playing with!

310
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:29,460
He's powerful enough to destroy us all!

311
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:35,077
Make the necessary preparations
for the blood-feeding experiment.

312
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:36,880
And don't screw anything up!

313
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:39,077
Help us!

314
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,820
Let us do anything, please!

315
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:42,290
Hmm.

316
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:44,920
I have a proposal for you.

317
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:48,241
Go ahead and choose someone
from among yourselves.

318
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:52,920
We need blood for a very
important historic experiment.

319
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:57,397
Once you have all agreed on who will
be the one to sacrifice his life,

320
00:20:57,480 --> 00:21:00,715
we will grant the rest of
you your freedom immediately.

321
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:04,670
Me!

322
00:21:04,753 --> 00:21:06,080
I volunteer for it!

323
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:11,057
If I do your experiment, you promise
that you let everyone else go, right?

324
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:12,560
You are quite brave.

325
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:17,257
Courage like yours is a thing that
must be cultivated like a lush garden.

326
00:21:17,340 --> 00:21:19,752
Here, we allow only the most fit to live.

327
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:22,800
Set the boy aside and
execute everyone else.

328
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:46,060
Let the experiment begin!

329
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:11,597
I'll be the roundabout.

330
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:15,757
The words will make you out and out.

331
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:19,280
I'll spend the day your way.

332
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:23,857
Call it morning driving through the sun.

333
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:25,500
And in and out the valley.

334
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:38,597
The music dance and sing.

335
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:42,817
They make the children really ring.

336
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:47,000
I spend the day your way.

337
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,957
Call it moaning, driving through the sun.

338
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:52,740
And in and out the valley.

339
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:57,420
Then all around the lake.

340
00:22:58,540 --> 00:23:00,857
Milders come out of the sky.

341
00:23:00,940 --> 00:23:02,380
And they stand there.

342
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:09,320
One mile over, we'll be
there and we'll see you.

343
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:15,720
Ten two summers, we'll be
there and I'll be with you.

344
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:21,577
Twenty four and five
mile over, we'll see you.

345
00:23:21,660 --> 00:23:24,060
I'll be there with you.

346
00:23:28,540 --> 00:23:30,477
You've no idea what he's capable of!

347
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:33,177
All I've got under my skirt
is more tequila, big boy.

348
00:23:33,260 --> 00:23:36,477
Which one of you was fool
enough to disturb my slumber?

349
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:39,501
He's squeezing himself
into the ventilation, dogs!
